}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
February 26, 2004

\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The package is first loaded into ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(<< c:\\\\mathfemm\\\\mathfemm.m\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "With a single command, a peer-to-peer ",
  StyleBox["MathLink",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " connection to FEMM is established.  Since the connection is peer-to-peer, \
the user can manipulate FEMM either using ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " calls or by directly using the FEMM user interface, depending upon what \
the user perceives as simplest for the task at hand."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(OpenFEMM[]\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "There are ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " analogs for virtually all functionality that can be commanded through Lua \
scripting.  For example, a geometry could be completely constructed, \
analyzed, and post-processed using ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " functions that operate on an instance of FEMM."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
For the purposes of this demonstration, a previously solved problem will be \
loaded.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(OpenDocument["\<c:\\program \
files\\femm40\\examples\\KelvinTransformation.ans\>"]\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "A display of the FEMM solution can be programmatically incorporated into a \
",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " notebook:"
}], "Text"],

